cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aitrail, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "aitrail: Document, Verify and Disclose the Use of AI in Research"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
authors:
  - family-names: "Sánchez-Núñez"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7845-9506"
url: "https://pablosancheznunez.com/aitrail/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablosancheznunez/aitrail"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - research integrity
  - transparency
  - provenance
  - AI disclosure
  - open science
  - R
abstract: >-
  An R package that keeps a structured, version-controlled record of how AI
  tools are used in each phase of a research project, audits gaps in human
  oversight, checks references against Crossref and DataCite, and generates
  AI-use disclosure statements in English and Spanish.
